<title>ESTONIA: HOTEL OLUMPIA PROFIT UP IN MAY.</title>
<headline>HOTEL OLUMPIA PROFIT UP IN MAY.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hotel Olumpia, whose minority shares will be sold in a public offering, had profit before taxes of seven million kroons in May, it said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The figure was up from April's profit of four million kroons.</p>
<p>&quot;In May and June two big client groups - businessmen and tourists - are active,&quot; chairman Tarmo Sumberg told Reuters.</p>
<p>Sumberg added that the hotel also expects a strong profit figure in June.</p>
<p>Olumpia had turnover of 19 million kroons in May, up from 16.3 million kroons the previous month.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
